    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16867" root="رهف" body-key="r">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَهُفَ</span></b> , aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَهُفَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَهَافَةٌ</span> (JK, MA, K) and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَهَفٌ</span> (JK, K) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَهْفٌ</span>, (TA,) <i>It</i> (a sword, K,
or a thing [of any kind], JK, TA) <i>was,</i> or <i>became,
thin,</i> and <i>slender;</i> (JK, K, TA;) <i>it</i> (a sword)
<i>was,</i> or <i>became, thin in the edge</i> or <i>point;</i> (Ham
p. 349;) <i>it was,</i> or <i>became, sharp,</i> or <i>keen; contr.
of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَلَّ</span>. (MA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَهَفَهُ</span>: see what next follows.

